The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
nvmet_passthru_override_id_ctrl(req);
nvmet_passthru_override_id_ns(req);
nvmet_passthru_override_id_descs(req);
```
Reason:
The id override functions are called without capturing their return status, meaning any errors or issues encountered during their execution are not reported back to the caller. This oversight can lead to undetected errors during command processing, potentially resulting in incorrect behavior or system instability.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
status = nvmet_passthru_override_id_ctrl(req);
status = nvmet_passthru_override_id_ns(req);
status = nvmet_passthru_override_id_descs(req);
```
Reason:
By assigning the return value of the id override functions to the `status` variable, the patch ensures that any errors encountered during their execution are captured and can be propagated back to the caller. This allows for proper error handling and reporting, improving the reliability of the NVMe passthru functionality.

